/// Deterministic ECDSA signature generation over P-521 with HMAC with the hash function `hash` names (RFC 6979 §3.2; FIPS 186-5 §6.4.1): with the private key `d` (66 bytes, most significant first), signs the hash `digest` (`hLen` bytes, the length of `hash`'s values), deriving the per-message secret number `k` from the key and the hash. Returns 1 and writes `r` then `s` (66 bytes each, most significant first) to `*out`; or returns 0 and writes zeros to `*out` if `d` is not in `[1, n-1]`, or if none of the first 8 candidates for `k` is suitable (which does not happen in practice). `hash` names the hash function: 1 SHA-1, 2 SHA-224, 3 SHA-256, 4 SHA-384, 5 SHA-512, 6 SHA-512/224, 7 SHA-512/256 (`VG.Spec.HashId`, as `VG.Spec.RsaPkcs1Sig.Hash.ofId` numbers them).
///
/// Contract: `VG.Spec.Ecdsa.Rfc6979.Instance.signAnyContract`. Constant time but for the number of candidates for `k` tried (almost always 1): timing may depend on the pointers, `hash`, `digest_len` and that number, not otherwise on the key or the hash.
///
